# STOCKTAKE_PIPELINE_LOCKED — periods, counts, PDFs (all locations)

Marker tag: `STOCKTAKE_PIPELINE_LOCKED` (enforced by `scripts/verifyStocktakeLockMarkers.js` on build).

**AI agents:** Treat stocktake / period / variance / PDF logic as **frozen** until the product owner **explicitly** requests a change in the chat (e.g. "change variance PDF", "update stocktake period close"). Incidental bugs elsewhere do **not** justify edits here.

Read **`docs/stocktake-pdf-pipeline.md`** before any authorized touch.

## Locked scope

- **PDFs:** opening, closing, variance, aggregation review, count sheet; auto-download on submit; manual period PDF buttons.
- **Periods & counts:** `stock_periods`, opening/closing stock entries, stocktake events/counts, rollover submit in `api/stocktake.js`.
- **Ledger:** `stocktakeVarianceLedger.js`, `buildVarianceRows`, `reconcileInventoryFromVariance`.
- **Data in variance (all future periods):** period **sales** from POS (`sales` + `sales_items` for the period `location_id`); **transfers** from `stock_transfer_sessions` / `stock_transfer_entries` (`sumTransfers` — **approved** on `/transfers` plus legacy null-status product-list sessions).

## Automation (no manual work per period)

Rollover close → `buildVarianceRows` → inventory reconcile → closing + variance + next opening PDFs. Opening/closing re-downloads use the same variance rows (imputed opening when needed).

## Rules

- **All locations** — no per-outlet forks.
- **Forbidden** without explicit owner command: any edit to manifest files in `docs/stocktake-pdf-pipeline.md`, refactors, formatting, or "improvements".
- **Authorized changes only:** update the doc + run `node scripts/verifyStocktakeVarianceLedger.js` and `node scripts/verifyStocktakeTransferVariance.js`; keep lock markers (`STOCKTAKE_PIPELINE_LOCKED`) in touched files.

File-pattern rule: `.cursor/rules/stocktake-locked-files.mdc` (applies when those paths are open/edited).
